d"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIMQNvvCya66a6YyDlxwkxjjJPN3uaFI+QD3OjyC8e1UF rebar-mac-492a5c71 joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com 20261119"},{"content_hash":"1e72806d619d7cfbf8d0a5ff5a721e32de5bdf5ae44ccd8c11a76b76dd759fce","event_uuid":"279e32eb-d1a0-4760-86dd-75ce13334c17","position":{"commit_sha":"eb0e6133076d609c45e56ae62c2619133115fd2a","position":"1795235690433055001-279e32eb-d1a0-4760-86dd-75ce13334c17"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIMQNvvCya66a6YyDlxwkxjjJPN3uaFI+QD3OjyC8e1UF rebar-mac-492a5c71 joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com 20261119"},{"content_hash":"76cc65e35e8a38f1f7d1e80d19b1582a6ffc3981facdb0c987c555acb1bf21e7","event_uuid":"2683f587-06ff-4ab8-b598-7dc6fce610f2","position":{"commit_sha":"3224b29d39905a54ce871992fe81f59db0a85367","position":"1795235763318062001-2683f587-06ff-4ab8-b598-7dc6fce610f2"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIMQNvvCya66a6YyDlxwkxjjJPN3uaFI+QD3OjyC8e1UF rebar-mac-492a5c71 joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com 20261119"},{"content_hash":"e969bb87fcdee53dd110a40e136584a6e674ecadbb2041ea0cf7940b7d66cf40","event_uuid":"bb144a0b-ba30-4b83-82be-881d2867f1fa","position":{"commit_sha":"3224b29d39905a54ce871992fe81f59db0a85367","position":"1795235775057546001-bb144a0b-ba30-4b83-82be-881d2867f1fa"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIMQNvvCya66a6YyDlxwkxjjJPN3uaFI+QD3OjyC8e1UF rebar-mac-492a5c71 joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com 20261119"},{"content_hash":"5a6ae007161eb5f0c37f34c4e6903c3035958f3a725483caceb84b11403c7f58","event_uuid":"74c12f06-f9ff-4fda-8094-c5f198c5d528","position":{"commit_sha":"6ba00f8075f9ee3d55b2c80573ee93a78b949357","position":"1795236205742275001-74c12f06-f9ff-4fda-8094-c5f198c5d528"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIMQNvvCya66a6YyDlxwkxjjJPN3uaFI+QD3OjyC8e1UF rebar-mac-492a5c71 joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com 20261119"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":"claude-code_2-1-311_agent","claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":"05f74084-8156-4489-b43f-fbb9222cdc20","comments":[{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Root-cause investigation (worktree fix-finwhale at 459ad3874dd). (1) With the read-path reconverge throttle marker absent, rebar.comment on a superseded clone SUCCEEDS on current main: emit_cross_session_warning -> show_ticket -> reads.ensure_fresh -> sync.reconverge runs the stale-clone override before finalize_event. (2) With the marker stamped as just-run (a read in the last 60 s, the normal state of a busy MCP server), the same write is refused as DIVERGED. That is the CLI/MCP difference. (3) Experiment: making write_blocking_divergence return None when the remote epoch supersedes local lets the write commit, but the event never reaches the remote: push non-FF -> push_recovery merge of the unrelated history fails 5 times ('merge conflict'). So the original Fix section was insufficient; plan revised to also route push recovery through the existing override. Acceptance criteria unchanged.","timestamp":1795233579374003001},{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Plan revised after review-plan PASS-with-advisories (run 1): heal the superseded clone before the event is composed (sync.reconverge from the write entry points) instead of committing then overriding in push recovery. Advisories showed the push-recovery route would silently discard the new write when an older unpushed event predates the reclaim horizon, would bypass push's git seam, and would change completion_delivery's private-ref merges. AC block unchanged. Re-running review-plan.","timestamp":1795234627439374001},{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Implemented in worktree fix-finwhale: freshness.write_blocking_divergence flags superseded:true; new freshness.heal_superseded_clone runs sync.reconverge for a superseded clone; called from _seam.append_event (outside a batch) and txn.transition_core/claim_core before the lock; docs/concurrency.md updated. Red/green: tests/interfaces/store/test_write_after_reclaim.py has 5 tests; with src change reverted 4 fail with 'ticket write refused ... DIVERGED' (comment, old-unpushed-event comment, transition, claim) and the unrelated-remote refusal passes; with the fix all 5 pass. Related suites (stale_clone_override, gate_store_freshness, fsck_push_pending, push_strict): 64 passed. make lint and make typecheck pass. Next: make verify.","timestamp":1795236205742275001}],"created_at":1795229114016447001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"8150312d-4f4e-44a9-bbf6-c56ae8e97058","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"536b-8930-b922-4063"}],"description":"## Problem\n\nAfter a reclaim publish-swap, a clone whose `origin/tickets` was already fetched to the rewritten baseline refuses every ticket write as DIVERGED, even though the remote's store epoch provably supersedes the local one and `_store/sync.py::_override_if_reclaimed` would move the clone onto the new history.\n\nObserved 2026-11-20 PST after publishing 6a6dda16fc7: the box MCP server's first write (`comment_ticket`) failed with \"ticket write refused: the local ticket store has DIVERGED from the shared store with no shared ancestor\". The same write through the local CLI succeeded and the sync logged \"clone moved onto reclaimed remote … replayed 0 unpushed event(s)\". The MCP clone had to be reset by hand.\n\n## Cause (reproduced)\n\n`_commands/_seam.py::finalize_event` calls `_refuse_unpublishable_store` → `_store/freshness.py::write_blocking_divergence`, which returns `diverged` whenever `merge-base HEAD <remote>/<branch>` fails. It never consults `compat.remote_epoch_supersedes_local`, and nothing on the write path runs the stale-clone override itself.\n\nWhy the CLI write healed and the MCP write did not: a write reaches `sync.reconverge` (fetch + override) only through the read path's `reads.ensure_fresh`, which the CLI runs before every write arm and the library write runs via `emit_cross_session_warning` → `show_ticket`. That reconverge is throttled to once per 60 s by a marker file. A short-lived CLI process whose marker is old reconverges first and is moved onto the reclaimed baseline before `finalize_event` runs. A long-running MCP server that reads constantly is usually inside the 60 s window, so its write skips the reconverge and the precheck is the first code to see the already-fetched superseded ref. Reproduction in a throwaway repo with a real bare origin: with the marker stamped as just-run, `rebar.comment` refuses with DIVERGED on current main; with the marker absent, the same write succeeds. What fetched the box's ref without the override running (for example an idle-sync round that found the write lock busy, or an earlier push-recovery fetch) was not established from the box.\n\nRejected fix (tested): only making the precheck return `None` for a superseded clone lets the event commit on the superseded history, but it never reaches the remote. The push is rejected as non-fast-forward and `_store/push_recovery.py::_merge_remote_under_lock` tries to merge the unrelated reclaimed history (5 attempts, each \"merge conflict\").\n\n## Approach\n\nHeal the superseded clone BEFORE the event is composed, instead of committing on the superseded history and repairing during push. Committing first would hand the new event to the stale-clone override, which discards every unpushed event (the new one included) when the clone's oldest unpushed event predates the reclaim horizon, and it would need a second override path inside push recovery (which completion delivery also uses for private-ref merges).\n\n- `_store/freshness.py::write_blocking_divergence` additionally reports `superseded: true` on its `diverged` verdict when `compat.remote_epoch_supersedes_local(tracker, <remote_ref commit>)` holds. The verdict is still `diverged`, so anything the heal could not repair is still refused.\n- New `_store/freshness.py::heal_superseded_clone(tracker, repo_root)`: when that verdict is `superseded`, run `_store/sync.py::reconverge(tracker)`, the existing sync round (fetch, take the write lock, `_override_if_reclaimed`). That backs the tip up under `refs/rebar/stale-override/`, resets onto the reclaimed baseline, and replays fresh unpushed events. Best-effort: it never raises; a fetch failure, busy lock, unreadable horizon config or failed override leaves the clone as it was, and the precheck then refuses as today.\n- Call it from the write entry points that do not yet hold the write lock: `_commands/_seam.py::_append_event_body` before `finalize_event` (outside a batch, matching the precheck's own batch rule), and `_commands/txn.py::transition_core` / `claim_core` before `_acquire_write_lock` (they reduce fresh state under the lock, so moving HEAD first is safe). The new event then commits on top of the reclaimed baseline and pushes as a fast-forward through the unchanged push path.\n- `finalize_event`'s precheck keeps its behaviour: an unrelated remote (lineage does not name the local epoch), or a superseded clone the heal could not move, is still refused as DIVERGED before any commit.\n- No new config key, env var or flag. `push_recovery.py` is not changed.\n\n## Scope\n\nIn: `src/rebar/_store/freshness.py`, `src/rebar/_commands/_seam.py`, `src/rebar/_commands/txn.py`, and a new regression test module. Out: the atomic completion close (`completion_txn`, which pins the tickets OID before taking the lock), delete and reconciler-inbound writes; these keep today's refusal on a superseded clone until a read or idle-sync round moves it. Also out: gate-read freshness (`store_freshness`) and the 60 s read throttle.\n\n## Testing\n\nNew `tests/interfaces/store/test_write_after_reclaim.py` drives the library against a real bare origin that a parentless baseline replaced, with the read-path throttle marker stamped as just-run so the write path is the first code to see the superseded ref:\n- `rebar.comment` on a clone whose remote lineage names its epoch lands on the remote tip on top of that baseline. Fails on current main with \"ticket write refused … DIVERGED\".\n- The same with an older-than-horizon unpushed local event: the new comment still lands, and the old event is kept under the stale-override backup ref.\n- `rebar.transition` open → in_progress on a superseded clone lands on the remote.\n- A baseline whose lineage names another epoch is still refused as DIVERGED, with neither the clone nor the remote moved.\n\nExisting `tests/unit/test_stale_clone_override.py`, `tests/unit/test_gate_store_freshness.py` and `tests/interfaces/store/test_fsck_push_pending.py` must stay green, then `make verify`.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] A regression test builds a clone on epoch A, a remote rewritten to epoch B whose lineage names A, fetches the remote ref, and performs a ticket write through the shared seam: the write succeeds and the event is on the remote tip. The test fails on current main.\n- [ ] A remote with an unrelated history (lineage does not name the local epoch) is still refused as DIVERGED.\n- [ ] `make verify` passes.","env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_store/freshness.py","reason":"flag a superseded clone on the write verdict; heal it through sync.reconverge"},{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/_seam.py","reason":"heal a superseded clone before composing an appended event"},{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/txn.py","reason":"heal a superseded clone before transition/claim take the write lock"},{"path":"tests/interfaces/store/test_write_after_reclaim.py","reason":"regression tests: superseded clone writes land on remote; unrelated remote still refused"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"2683f587-06ff-4ab8-b598-7dc6fce610f2","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"releases":[],"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"3f6c-44e8-b0e4-4f68","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Write precheck refuses a clone a reclaim superseded","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["fae4fd5f-b8cf-49ee-b8b7-a856b748283d","8150312d-4f4e-44a9-bbf6-c56ae8e97058","d4867d55-5417-4ad4-af41-19bfbe1fe627","085ddb68-98b4-42e5-9b4d-275988e92ee5","827ec5fc-8373-4b53-822a-5fb1d0b7a547","1d98ad38-9116-46d9-a573-339a3b398150","140dc8fa-9090-4280-b05b-af3cd97c5d53","f69a42bc-8cba-4110-8a3b-9661665575b8","97bfa4f4-a58e-4e48-b02f-dd0ad5fb22dd","279e32eb-d1a0-4760-86dd-75ce13334c17","2683f587-06ff-4ab8-b598-7dc6fce610f2","bb144a0b-ba30-4b83-82be-881d2867f1fa","74c12f06-f9ff-4fda-8094-c5f198c5d528"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1795236205742275002,"uuid":"b92805ce-4dbb-4e6c-b7f1-6f61ae2b4943"}